## Context

The first acceptance milestone is one project, one small shared snapshot and one adapter. Select the first runtime based on accessible representative execution evidence; record the choice rather than promising all runtimes at once.

Design baseline: v6, merged by PR #903. See `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md` and `docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`. This planning change implements nothing and closes no work.

## Relevant files

Library/CLI from 0911–0922; selected runtime integration points; existing startup/prompt hooks; `rules/knowledge-hints.md`.

## Actions

1. Implement a thin event/delivery adapter with one owner per component and no duplicated memory policy.
2. Protect canonical bodies from native writers. Disclose uncontrollable native-memory interference; no three-mode configuration or importer.
3. Trigger task recall once the task is sufficiently clear and before its first relevant consequential action; refresh on material task or constraint changes without requiring a user recall request. Record supported start/task/pre-action/resume/child/compaction boundaries and a small delivery record outside model summaries. Rebuild bundles and reset duplicate suppression according to context retained after compaction, not everything ever sent.
4. Run in a disposable offline clone. Test logical bundle replacement and cumulative cost where old injected text cannot be removed.

## Test

Live smoke verifies actual delivered context, not just a required sentence in a skill. Inject, compact where supported, retract and resume: verify correction delivery and no stale re-injection. Show explicit reduced guarantees for unavailable hooks. Verify pre-action recall and material-task-change refresh, including repeated changes within bounded active allocation and measured cumulative transcript cost.

## Verification

- [ ] Run the focused fixtures and show they detect the relevant failure.
- [ ] Run applicable repository checks; record commands, results and limitations.
- [ ] Confirm the implementation matches this scope and v6, including explicit capability limits.

## Invariants

- Canonical bodies and provenance remain reviewable; memory cannot override decisions.
- No mandatory residency, automatic generalisation, new native-memory modes or policy duplication.
- Use the common library and normal Git integration; no runtime implementation is part of the planning PR.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] One runtime demonstrates orientation, recent supplement and task recall end to end.
- [ ] Fresh clone needs no original home directory or shared service.
- [ ] Ownership, boundaries, budget accounting and limitations documented from evidence.
